>
That's the reasonable answer, backed up by the parsing structure.

A related point is that quantifiers in a be-argument shouldn't be
exportable to the main prenex, because they belong to the definition of the
new selbri created by "be". This can be used to give a quantifier that
appears later in the sentence scope over one that appeared earlier, but
inside a be-argument.

